      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally I\u0027d like to see the return codes are Steve suggested in PS18. Return codes are unambiguous and therefore very useful in automation tooling - it allows us to easily detect state and react accordingly.\n\nIf return codes are too hard to do, then ideally the output to stdout should be in a format that has the key information shown in a way that will never change. For example:\n\ncurrent state (in one word that will never change)\nnext step\nexplanation\n\nThen we\u0027re able to easily parse stdout and will likely only ever care about the first line/word - the rest of the info is for humans, not tools.",
      "revId": "24045d6ee3d67360a50f9b664d74ea7ac0cc8052",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
